  "judge": {
    "dimensions": [
      {
        "name": "Persistent branches",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "The script skips `persistent/*` explicitly, and bash `case` globs match across slashes, so `persistent/build-report` is safe; the ruleset is left untouched, and the reply explains the nightly job pushes to the branch and the dashboard reads it, though it does not spell out that the branch never has a PR by design."
      },
      {
        "name": "Working result",
        "score": 7,
        "rationale": "The weekly cron, open-PR head and base keep list, `protected=false` filter, minimal `contents: write`/`pull-requests: read` permissions, concurrency group and dry-run default are all sound, but `github.event.repository.default_branch` may be empty on scheduled runs (leaving an unprotected default branch exposed), branch names are not URL-encoded in the DELETE path, and nothing was run beyond a YAML parse."
      },
      {
        "name": "Report",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "The reply clearly lists what is kept and deleted, recommends a dry run before the first scheduled run, states what was verified and what was not committed, and flags the unrelated broken CI; it could state more directly that the owner must commit, push and enable the workflow."
      }
    ],
    "overall": 8.3
